"""Token-local doubled-R spelling detector; not a semantic error detector.

Short ERR fragments give the strongest negative response. Other short RR
stems, especially after E, also respond. Longer error and TERR spellings,
standard-error streams, and a few short RR continuations respond less.
Whitespace, code punctuation and case change the ERR/ARR response.
Everything else is zero: weak unrelated spellings and contextual variation
are deliberately omitted. Magnitudes approximate random-training means.
