Backtick runs respond most strongly, particularly after blank lines or colons.
Their strength depends on whether a token begins or continues a run and whether
it includes a line ending. Language labels and the line ending of a code-fence
header also respond; document-initial fences receive an extra boost.
Smaller rules cover tilde separators, HTML code markup,
syntax-highlighting labels and LaTeX display environments. Everything else is 0.
Ordinary prose and code content are not modeled beyond these markers.
The short text tail and backtick-run state reset at each document boundary.
